<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25409" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jussus</span></b> , ūs (used only in
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>abl.
			sing.</i>), m.
			jubeo, <i>an order, command, decree</i>
			(class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tuo jussu profectus sum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Curc. 2, 3, 50</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Jovis jussu venio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Am. prol. 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestro jussu coactus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Imp. Pomp. 9, 26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aut ab regibus lecti aut post reges exactos
					jussu populi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					4, 4, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sine populi jussu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sall. C. 29, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Romano jussu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 9, 2, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Timotheus populi jussu bellum gessit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nep.
					Timoth. 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Neronis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					10, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">patris dominive negotium gerere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gai. Inst. 4, 70</span></i>
			.</div>
